$ SOFiSTiK MCP self-test: steel cantilever HEA 200, length 6 m (6 elements), tip load 1 kN.
$ Hand calculation: tip deflection = P L^3/(3 E Iy) + P L/(G Az), fixed-end moment = P L = 6 kNm,
$ support reaction = 1 kN.  selftest.py compares these with what the MCP server reads from the .cdb.

+PROG AQUA urs:1
HEAD MCP self-test cantilever
NORM DC "DIN" NDC "EN199X-200X" COUN 49
STEE 1 S 355
SECT 1 ; PROF TYPE HEA 200
END

+PROG SOFIMSHA urs:2
HEAD MCP self-test cantilever
UNIT 5 $ sections in mm, geometry and loads in m
SYST TYPE SPAC GDIV 1000
NODE NO X Y Z FIX
  1 0 0 0 F
  2 1 0 0
  3 2 0 0
  4 3 0 0
  5 4 0 0
  6 5 0 0
  7 6 0 0
GRP 0
BEAM NO 1 NA 1 NE 2 NCS 1
BEAM NO 2 NA 2 NE 3 NCS 1
BEAM NO 3 NA 3 NE 4 NCS 1
BEAM NO 4 NA 4 NE 5 NCS 1
BEAM NO 5 NA 5 NE 6 NCS 1
BEAM NO 6 NA 6 NE 7 NCS 1
END

+PROG SOFILOAD urs:3
HEAD MCP self-test load
UNIT 5 $ sections in mm, geometry and loads in m
LC 1 TYPE 'NONE' TITL 'self-test tip load 1 kN'
  NODE 7 TYPE PZ 1.0
END

+PROG ASE urs:4
HEAD MCP self-test linear analysis
LC 1
END
